// Personality — a small set of curated *motives* (after Reiss / CK3): continuous
// drives an agent carries, that a goal's appeal can read by name. There is no
// hardwired trait: add one here and reference it from a goal's considerations
// (`(input: Trait("vengeance"), curve: ...)`).
//
// A trait is INNATE — who you are. Unlike a skill it does not grow by doing or
// decay from disuse. Each agent is born near the `baseline`, varied by `spread`,
// and a trait changes only through significant life events (see appraisals.ron),
// whose effect persists. Fast, transient feeling lives in the separate mood layer.
//
// Traits may come in opposed pairs: an event that raises one lowers its `opposes`
// by the same amount (you can't grow more vengeful and more forgiving at once).
//
//   baseline  the drive's innate value across the population (0..1)
//   spread    how far an individual's birth value varies around it (±)
//   opposes   the trait this one is the opposite of (optional)
[
    (name: "ambition",    baseline: 0.20, spread: 0.20, opposes: Some("contentment")),
    (name: "contentment", baseline: 0.50, spread: 0.20, opposes: Some("ambition")),
    (name: "vengeance",   baseline: 0.20, spread: 0.15, opposes: Some("forgiveness")),
    (name: "forgiveness", baseline: 0.45, spread: 0.20, opposes: Some("vengeance")),
    (name: "greed",       baseline: 0.30, spread: 0.20),
    (name: "sociability", baseline: 0.50, spread: 0.20),
    (name: "piety",       baseline: 0.40, spread: 0.20),
    (name: "caution",     baseline: 0.40, spread: 0.20),

    // ── The achlydesan register — a soul's standing toward its own captivity ──────────
    // Achlydesa is a counterfeit world (the mist over a dying eye), shaped and ruled by a
    // blind false god and his seven Archons; its souls are the dead who do not know they
    // have died. These dispositions decide whether a soul sinks into the dream or claws
    // toward waking. NONE is read by a bundled survival goal, so they perturb no economy —
    // the deeper layers read them: dialogue, the director's beats (the Demiurge myth), and
    // the Archon Law in `norms.ron`.
    //
    // gnosis ↔ oblivion — the pull to *wake* (to know the world for the prison it is)
    // against the pull to *forget* (to drink the mist and be content in the counterfeit).
    // Most are born asleep: gnosis sits low, oblivion high. Sustained `longing` quickens
    // gnosis; a life of `despair` deepens oblivion (see moods.ron).
    (name: "gnosis",     baseline: 0.10, spread: 0.10, opposes: Some("oblivion")),
    (name: "oblivion",   baseline: 0.55, spread: 0.20, opposes: Some("gnosis")),
    // defiance ↔ submission — whether a soul resists the Archons' order or bows to it. The
    // defiant flout the Law (norms.ron) where it forbids ascending or freeing the bound.
    (name: "defiance",   baseline: 0.20, spread: 0.18, opposes: Some("submission")),
    (name: "submission", baseline: 0.50, spread: 0.20, opposes: Some("defiance")),
    // devotion — zeal for the blind god and his cult, the fervour the temples manufacture
    // (cf. `rapture`, the bliss they feed it on). Distinct from `piety`, the quieter awe of
    // an unseen hand that is the seed of the myth.
    (name: "devotion",   baseline: 0.30, spread: 0.22),

    // ── More motives — broader dimensions of who a soul is, for the dialogue and director
    // layers to read. (Still unread by any bundled survival goal, so the economy is untouched.)
    //
    // curiosity — the itch to look closer at the seams of the world; a softer kin of gnosis
    // that doesn't yet know what it is looking for.
    (name: "curiosity",  baseline: 0.35, spread: 0.20),
    // wanderlust ↔ rootedness — the pull to roam the mist and find new ground against the
    // pull to stay, to hold one place against the fog. (The waypoints exist to be sought.)
    (name: "wanderlust",  baseline: 0.30, spread: 0.20, opposes: Some("rootedness")),
    (name: "rootedness",  baseline: 0.45, spread: 0.20, opposes: Some("wanderlust")),
    // cruelty ↔ compassion — whether a soul adds to the world's suffering or eases it. The
    // Archons' work is cruelty wearing the face of order.
    (name: "cruelty",     baseline: 0.20, spread: 0.18, opposes: Some("compassion")),
    (name: "compassion",  baseline: 0.45, spread: 0.20, opposes: Some("cruelty")),
    // pride ↔ humility — how a soul carries itself before the others and the unseen hand.
    (name: "pride",       baseline: 0.35, spread: 0.20, opposes: Some("humility")),
    (name: "humility",    baseline: 0.40, spread: 0.20, opposes: Some("pride")),
    // zeal — the heat a soul brings to whatever it believes, holy or heretical alike.
    (name: "zeal",        baseline: 0.25, spread: 0.22),
]
